users/kingjaceo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T02:09:48Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T02:09:48Z","body":"> [@kingjaceo](https://github.com/kingjaceo) that should not be necessary. The signals in the editor should have been working since 4.4-dev7.\n> \n> Have you tried deleting and re-creating the connections in the editor in beta3? If that fixes it then I guess you had some bad state left over from dev6 which isn't a problem going forward as nobody should be using dev6. If it's still an issue then something is wrong, but FYI it works for me.\n\nReconnecting things after updating seems to fix the issue. Thanks a ton!!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646767692/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646811049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100097#issuecomment-2646811049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100097","id":2646811049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dwyGp","user":{"login":"kingjaceo","id":44843586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODQzNTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44843586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo","html_url":"https://github.com/kingjaceo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingjaceo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T02:57:37Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T02:57:37Z","body":"> Delete `.godot/exported` folder.\n\nBut apparently it doesn't always work? On another scene I had with an in-editor signal connection, I tried disconnecting and reconnecting but it wouldn't work. So I deleted `exported`, which solved the problem there. Thanks!!!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646811049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646814025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100097#issuecomment-2646814025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100097","id":2646814025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dwy1J","user":{"login":"mgiuca","id":228433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODQzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca","html_url":"https://github.com/mgiuca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T03:00:57Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T03:00:57Z","body":"Oh yeah... if you go back to my original bug report, this was part of the issue. dev6 did not just have broken exports, it corrupted the .godot directory. Note that I said if you make a connection in dev6 then downgrade to dev5, it will still be broken until you delete your .godot directory.\n\nSo that fact that you had to do that after updating to beta3 is expected. It won't be a problem for anyone upgrading from 4.3 to 4.4 stable as they will skip over dev6, so not a problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646814025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148784364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100097#issuecomment-3148784364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100097","id":3148784364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67rqLs","user":{"login":"fahall","id":5201085,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDEwODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5201085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall","html_url":"https://github.com/fahall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fahall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-03T23:50:14Z","updated_at":"2025-08-03T23:50:14Z","body":"I think this may have regressed in 4.4.1 stable (or partial regression). \n\nI just spent a stupid amount of time debugging lost connections in scenes that only happen if:\n1. Signal added _via editor_ in 4.4.1\n2. Project is exported (signals work fine when running from editor)\n3. The observer function is wired _via the editor_. Anything wired in code worked as expected. I assume this means something is lost in the .tscn export process.\n\nSome notes:\n1. I'm using the .NET version of 4.4.1 stable\n2. Upgrading to 4.5-beta4 did not immediately fix the problem.\n3. In 4.5-beta4, if I delete the signals, delete .godot contents, and then create the signals again (no visible change in git), then they work fine again upon export. \n4. Only the signals for which I follow the steps in #3 actually get fixed. Any other broken signals remain broken. \n5. I know that broken signals are all firing (I'm logging calls from them that I wire in code). ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148784364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]